Add support for excluding paths removed from lite Chromium tarballs

This allows Electron patches to be applied against Chromium lite tarballs
(generated by chromium-tarballs/package_chromium.sh) which have mobile and
test-only directories removed. When ELECTRON_USE_LITE_EXCLUDES=1 is set,
git-am will skip hunks that modify files in these excluded directories.

The exclude list matches the prune_lite_excluded_dirs() function in:
https://github.com/chromium-linux-tarballs/chromium-tarballs

--- a/electron/script/apply_all_patches.py
+++ b/electron/script/apply_all_patches.py
@@ -12,6 +12,96 @@
 
